  "description": "Event-balance variant of Cavalla's 19 Jun 1944 Philippine Sea approach. Same cast as the museum tight seed (NPC Sh\u014dkaku SE-bound ~135\u00b0 recovering at 18 kn; NPC Zeke CAP loitering ~1.5 nm to port; playable Asashio-class Urakaze starboard; playable Gato USS Cavalla at PD 18 m) but Cavalla opens ~4 nm on the carrier's starboard bow — about 2.4 nm ahead along the track and 3.2 nm off to starboard (not beam, not turn-1 TDC ready). If Cavalla holds, the formation takes about 8 minutes to draw abeam, so the boat can wait and maneuver and Urakaze has time to turn and sweep sonar (the sub starts outside the forward search cone). Clock 11:00. Passwords: umpire / red (Urakaze) / blue (Cavalla); tokens urakaze-demo / cavalla-demo. Pair with cavalla-shokaku-philippine-sea for the historical tight geometry.",
